<h2>Monday, November 15,  2004</h2>	
<div class="post">
	 <h3 class="storytitle" id="post-38"><a href="http://www.marksportal.net/index.php?p=38" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: If God is for us&#8230;">If God is for us&#8230;</a></h3>
	<div class="meta">posted by: Mark @ 1:42 pm </div>
	
	<div id="wplinks" class="storycontent">
			<p><i>&#8220;&#8230;If God is for us, who is against us?&#8221;  (<a href="http://bible1.crosswalk.com/OnlineStudyBible/bible.cgi?word=Romans+8:31&#038;section=2&#038;version=nas"> Romans  8:31</a>, NASB95)</i></p>
	<p>These famous words of Paul has often been an encouragement to believers everwhere.  These words rang in my ears today as I was reading the accounts of John and Jesus birth in Luke.  Jesus had just been born when an angel was sent to &#8220;shepherds living out in the fields nearby".   After telling the shepherds of Jesus&#8217; birth&#8230;</p>
	<p><i>&#8220;Suddenly a great company of the heavenly host appeared with the angel, praising God and saying,</p>
	<p>&#8216;Glory to God in the highest,<br />
and on earth peace to men<br />
on whom his favor rests&#8217;&#8221;   (<a href="http://bible1.crosswalk.com/OnlineStudyBible/bible.cgi?word=Luke+2:13-14&#038;section=2&#038;version=nas"> Luke 2:13-14</a>, NIV)</i></p>
	<p>The angels praised God, which I understand, however they did something else&#8230;they blessed men.   They wished that we would have peace.  This caused me to realize that it wasn&#8217;t just God that was looking out for us and wishing the best for us, but the angels in heaven as well!</p>
	</div>
	
